# Structured-data extraction from messy, realistic documents (Phase 1).
# Mix of contains/regex (single-field) and json_schema (full-record) tasks.
{"id": "extract-1", "prompt": "Extract the invoice total from this messy email thread:\n\n---\nhey team, forwarding this from accounts payable, please process asap!!\n\nFrom: billing@acmesupplies.com\nSubject: Invoice #INV-88213 overdue\n\nHi,\n\nThis is a reminder that invoice INV-88213 for the March office supplies\norder (stapers, toner, paper) remains unpaid. Amount due incl. tax: $482.50.\nPlease remit within 10 days to avoid a late fee.\n\nThanks,\nAcme Supplies Billing\n---\n\nWhat is the total amount due, including the currency symbol?", "expected": "$482.50", "match": "contains"}
{"id": "extract-2", "prompt": "Extract the callback phone number from this voicemail transcript:\n\n\"Hi, this is Dana from the Riverside clinic calling about your upcoming\nappointment. Give us a call back whenever you get a chance, the number\nhere is (555) 234-7781, ask for scheduling. Thanks, bye!\"\n\nWhat is the phone number, in the same format it was spoken?", "expected": "\\(?555\\)?[-.\\s]?234[-.\\s]?7781", "match": "regex"}
{"id": "extract-3", "prompt": "Extract the tracking number from this shipping confirmation:\n\n\"Good news! Your package from NorthPeak Outdoor is on its way.\nOrder #NP-55219 shipped via GroundLine Express.\nTracking: 1Z-9F4-KQ2201-88\nEstimated delivery: Thursday.\"\n\nWhat is the tracking number?", "expected": "1Z-9F4-KQ2201-88", "match": "contains"}
{"id": "extract-4", "prompt": "Extract the date of the next meeting from these rambling notes:\n\n\"ok so we covered the Q3 roadmap, budget looks fine, marketing wants\nmore headcount which we'll revisit later. someone should follow up with\nlegal about the contract redline. next sync will be March 14th, same\ntime, same room. bring the updated deck.\"\n\nWhat date is the next meeting?", "expected": "March 14", "match": "contains"}
{"id": "extract-5", "prompt": "Parse this order confirmation into JSON. Reply with a fenced ```json block containing an object with fields: order_id (string), total (number), items (array of strings). Also repeat the compact JSON after an ANSWER: line.\n\n---\nThanks for your order!!\nOrder confirmation #ORD-77410\nItems: wireless mouse, USB-C hub, 2x notebook\nOrder total (tax incl.): $64.97\nShips within 2 business days.\n---", "expected": "", "match": "json_schema", "schema": {"type": "object", "required": ["order_id", "total", "items"], "properties": {"order_id": {"type": "string"}, "total": {"type": "number"}, "items": {"type": "array"}}}}
{"id": "extract-6", "prompt": "Extract the email address from this resume snippet:\n\n\"JORDAN LEE\nSenior Data Analyst | 5 years experience\nReach me anytime: jordan.lee92@careermail.com | (555) 019-2244\nPortfolio: jordanlee.dev\"\n\nWhat is the email address?", "expected": "[\\w.]+@[\\w.]+", "match": "regex"}
{"id": "extract-7", "prompt": "Extract the product name being complained about in this customer message:\n\n\"I've reached out twice already with no response. The SonicBrew Pro 12-cup\ncoffee maker I bought stopped heating water after 3 weeks. I want a refund\nor replacement, this is unacceptable for a $90 appliance.\"\n\nWhat product is the customer complaining about?", "expected": "SonicBrew Pro", "match": "contains"}
{"id": "extract-8", "prompt": "Parse this business card text into JSON. Reply with a fenced ```json block containing an object with fields: name (string), company (string), email (string). Also repeat the compact JSON after an ANSWER: line.\n\n---\nTAYLOR MORGAN\nHead of Partnerships\nBrightPath Logistics\ntaylor.morgan@brightpathlog.com | +1 (555) 882-1190\n---", "expected": "", "match": "json_schema", "schema": {"type": "object", "required": ["name", "company", "email"], "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "company": {"type": "string"}, "email": {"type": "string"}}}}
